From 8554b211fe75af7972b4617680965045b750d5d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Gierth <larsg@systemli.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:34:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] econet: en7528: add support for TP-Link EX20v v2

TP-Link EX20v v2 is an AX1800 ISP gateway based on the EcoNet EN7528.

* SoC: EcoNet EN7528 (MIPS 1004Kc, 2 cores / 4 threads)
* RAM: 512MiB (432MiB usable below the MMIO window)
* Flash: 512MiB SPI NAND, 4KiB page, 256KiB erase block
* WiFi: MT7915 DBDC on PCIe (the 0x7916 on pcie0 is its HIF2, left off)
* Ethernet: 1x WAN, 3x LAN on the EN7528 internal switch

The bootloader boots one of two kernel slots selected by an ASCII byte
at 0x240000 and does not verify the MD5/RSA fields of the TP-Link
kernel header, so a kernel wrapped in that header boots.

Layout: slot B (0x2980000) holds the main kernel, 0x2f80000-0x1c000000
is UBI (rootfs + overlay), slot A (0x380000) holds a small rescue
initramfs (tplink_ex20v-v2-rescue) used for the first install and
recovery.

LED/button GPIOs follow the EX20v (v1) port at
github.com/ozgunokan/openwrt-tplink-ex20v and still need verification
on v2.

